  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.83
  ==================================================

Removed a few [ANY KEY] hits, blank lines, and also added a couple of
spaces here and there to help smooth up the display.  Added a flag to
enable acknowledgement of a high score when 1) there was a header for
the score file, but 2) no scores were actually on the scoreboard!  In
addition added the YEAR number to the headers for buying and selling,
so now you can see what year you are in during play!  Expanded online
(I)nformation to explain in greater detail how to play the game, this
includes the ORE and MINE prices a player can expect.  Also, adjusted
the 'log' routine to send error messages, (if any), to a 'GMINER.err'
file in the directory where the Door.exe is, instead of looking for a
Metro log in the 'BBSfiles' directory.  Thanks PD!  PKN. 30-Nov-94.


  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.82
  ==================================================

Adjusted some of the game's variables which should now prevent values
getting below zero.  Increased the chances, by up to 20%, for a couple
of the nastier things, to NOT occur to a players colony, at least one
of which would always occur if certain conditions were true!  Revised
the RUDE word scanning a little for alias checks.  PKN. 29-Nov-94.


  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.81
  ==================================================

Few display changes.  Now defaults to [C]ontinue (so you can hit return
to continue game or press (M) for main menu.  Many DELAYs removed.  Few
screen clearing codes removed.  Stopped using Metro userlog for page
height setting, now uses hard-coded 23 lines per page.  This door will
run off TransAmiga BBS, BTW.

                                        - PFD 29-Nov-94

  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.80
  ==================================================

Altered the (I)nformation code to accept a [return] to be pressed or the
'N' key (as before) when you want to read the next page.  Previously, if
the [return] key was hit the same page would be printed.  Also noticed a
delay was needed after a user made it onto the scoreboard, and another
was added after a TOP score posted.  Also a clear screen was added prior
to displaying the high scores when a user completes a game, and is again
cleared before 'NEW GAME? (Y/n)' is asked thereafter.  PKN. 28-Nov-94.


  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.79
  ==================================================

Inserted a final time calculation into the lastuser routine to remove the
need for a full timecheck when quitting from the game.  PKN. 27-Nov-94.


  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.78
  ==================================================

Re-wrote startup to avoid Metro.config use.  Only needs to grab
SYSOPNAME, BBSNAME, WINDOWHEIGHT and WINDOWWIDTH anyway.  Changed serial
routine open_serial ever so slightly, cleaned up exit routine a little.

                                        - PFD 27-Nov-94

  ==================================================
   Changes and additions to note in GMINER V0.77
  ==================================================

Added (4) lines to the config file.  (LINEs 10-13)
==================================================
The setting on LINE 10: this sets the minimum user level which can access
the alias functions of GMINER. It ranges from 1-9 as per the OzMetro user
levels, and defaults to 2. Any user of user level less than the value you
put on this line will NOT be able to access the aliases functions at all.

The setting on LINE 11: this sets the minimum user level which will have
access to the 'lastusers' file of GMINER.  It ranges from 1-9 as per user
levels in OzMetro, and defaults to 1.  Any user who's level is less than
the value you set on this line will NOT be able to see the lastusers file.

The setting on LINE 12: this sets the maximum number of entries GMINER is
able to add to the highscore file before they start to scroll off.  This
value does NOT include the 3 line header.  So if you use 15 as the value
on this line, the highscore file will be actually 19 lines long, 3 lines
for the header, 15 score lines and an EOF marker on the last blank line.
Any value within the range 10-200 lines will be accepted.  The default is
for 34 score lines. (approx 2 NTSC screens or 1.5 PAL screens )

The setting on LINE 13: this sets the maximum number of entries GMINER is
able to add to the lastusers file before they start to scroll off.  This
value does NOT include the 3 line header.  So if you use 55 as the value
on this line, the lastusers file will be actually 59 lines long, 3 lines
for the header, 55 entries and an EOF marker on the last blank line.  Any
value within the range 10-500 lines will be accepted.  The default is set
for 100 lines.  (about 5 NTSC screens or 4 PAL screens worth.)

=====================================
Other changes in GMINER V0.77 to note
=====================================
Inserted the question "View scoreboard now?" after a user completes their
10 year term.   This is NOT dependant in any way on whether they actually
made it on the scoreboard however.  It does allow a user to finish a game
and see the scores (or not) and start a new game without having to return
to the menu to check how they went compared to all the other high scores.

=============================
Other changes in GMINER V0.77
=============================

None.

